ns2:CHEMONTID_0001410 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Xanthophylls" ;
    ns2:IAO_0000115 "Carotenoids containing an oxygenated carotene backbone. Carotenes are characterized by the presence of two end-groups (mostly cyclohexene rings, but also cyclopentene rings or acyclic groups) linked by a long branched alkyl chain. Carotenes belonging form a subgroup of the carotenoids family. Xanthophylls arise by oxygenation of the carotene backbone." ;
    ns1:hasBroadSynonym "C40 isoprenoids (tetraterpenes)",
        "Xanthophylls" ;
    ns1:hasOBONamespace "chemont" ;
    ns1:hasRelatedSynonym "a xanthophyll",
        "xanthophyll" ;
    ns1:id "CHEMONTID:0001410" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:CHEMONTID_0001277 .

ns2:CHEMONTID_0001575 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Retinoid esters" ;
    ns2:IAO_0000115 "Ester derivatives of retinoic acid. These are obtained by formal condensation of the hydroxy group of retinol with the carboxy group of any carboxylic acid." ;
    ns1:hasBroadSynonym "Retinoids" ;
    ns1:hasOBONamespace "chemont" ;
    ns1:hasRelatedSynonym "Retinoids",
        "retinyl ester" ;
    ns1:id "CHEMONTID:0001575" ;
    rdfs:comment """In humans, Diacylglycerol O-acyltransferase 1 (DGAT1) and Diacylglycerol O-acyltransferase 1 (DGAT2) also catalyze the reaction: Acyl-CoA + retinol = CoA + retinyl ester. They function as the major acyl-CoA retinol acyltransferase (ARAT) in the skin, where it acts to maintain retinoid homeostasis and prevent retinoid toxicity leading to skin and hair disorders. (UniProt)
In humans, Acyl-CoA wax alcohol acyltransferase 2 (AWAT2) may also have 2-acylglycerol O-acyltransferase (MGAT) and acyl-CoA:retinol acyltransferase (ARAT) activities, to catalyze the synthesis of diacylglycerols and retinyl esters; however this activity is unclear in vivo. (UniProt)""" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:CHEMONTID_0001606 .

